 /*
  * RUBY: the board's buttons, polled.
  *
- *   volume down  the SoC keypad controller, KP_MEM1 bit 0 (clear while down)
- *   volume up    MT6359 TOPSTATUS bit 3 (HOMEKEY_DEB, clear while down)
- *   power        MT6359 TOPSTATUS bit 1 (PWRKEY_DEB, clear while down)
+ * A34 (0902): the Galaxy A34 wires the volume keys the other way round:
+ *
+ *   volume up    the SoC keypad controller, KP_MEM1 bit 1 (clear while down)
+ *   volume down  MT6359P TOPSTATUS bit 3 (HOMEKEY_DEB, clear while down)
+ *   power        MT6359P TOPSTATUS bit 1 (PWRKEY_DEB, clear while down)
+ *
+ * and only the 20 ms poll is used (no legacy keypad interrupt: the A34's
+ * keypad interrupt is edge-triggered and the poll alone is enough).
  *
  * TOPSTATUS is the PMIC's debounced key level.  It is independent of the PSC
  * interrupt enable (0x910), so this driver never writes the PMIC; the boot
